---
// api-docs-read: static home page — no external API/protocol surface, only a booking link, mailto and optional form post.
// Home (site architecture doc, page type 12, 26 Nov 2026): AI for all work. Route a visitor in three clicks by work,
// industry, role or free tool. Research notes: one main button (the free diagnostic), the readiness check as the quiet
// second door, no headline stats, firm-level operator proof + method block for trust. Russell is named only on the About page.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ConsultingCta from '../components/ConsultingCta.astro';

const BOOK = 'https://calendly.com/zavient/call';

// Every kind of work with a guide gets a card. Work and industries without a guide yet share one line that points to
// the free diagnostic, which covers any workflow: no cards that jump straight to a booking page.
const kinds = [
  { href: '/ai-consulting/ai-automation-consulting.html', tag: 'Any team', title: 'Operations and workflows', text: 'Which handoffs, forms and approvals to automate first, and what good help looks like.' },
  { href: '/industries/law-firms.html', tag: 'Industry', title: 'Law firms', text: 'Research, review and first drafts. Lawyers keep the advice and the signature.' },
  { href: '/industries/manufacturing.html', tag: 'Industry', title: 'Manufacturing', text: 'Quality checks, maintenance and planning, with your floor leads in charge.' },
  { href: '/industries/supply-chain-logistics.html', tag: 'Industry', title: 'Supply chain and logistics', text: 'Forecasts, routing and the paperwork around every shipment.' },
  { href: '/ai-work/ai-construction-estimating.html', tag: 'Industry', title: 'Construction', text: 'Takeoffs and estimates you can check before you bid.' },
  { href: '/industries/insurance.html', tag: 'Industry', title: 'Insurance', text: 'Underwriting, claims and the reading around every file. People keep the call.' },
  { href: '/ai-work/ai-credit-scoring.html', tag: 'Industry', title: 'Banking and lending', text: 'Credit scoring you can explain to an examiner, then underwriting.' },
  { href: '#guides', tag: 'Any company', title: 'Finance and accounting', text: 'Invoices, month-end close, reconciliations and financial documents.' },
];
const noGuideYet = 'customer service, sales, HR, purchasing, IT, healthcare, or your industry';

// Role cards (8 cards, symmetrical 4x2 grid), operator first, owner-CEO and division heads included.
const roles = [
  { href: '/ai-consulting/ai-strategy-consulting.html', tag: 'COO', title: 'Which workflow should we fix first?', text: 'Which work pays back first, and what you should walk away with from outside help.' },
  { href: '/ai-work/account-reconciliation-automation.html', tag: 'Head of operations', title: 'What changes for my team?', text: 'Which tasks AI takes and who checks its work. Month-end close is the worked example.' },
  { href: '#work', tag: 'General manager', title: 'Can one team pilot it first?', text: 'Pick one kind of work below. Test it on one team before you scale.' },
  { href: '/ai-readiness-assessment.html', tag: 'Owner or CEO', title: 'Are we ready for AI at all?', text: 'A 3-minute check. It names your first project and the one gap to fix first.' },
  { href: '/industries/private-equity.html', tag: 'PE or holdco leader', title: 'Where does AI pay across portfolio firms?', text: 'Value creation plans, diligence, multi-entity close and portfolio monitoring.' },
  { href: '/ai-work/ai-credit-scoring.html', tag: 'Head of lending', title: 'Is it allowed, and does it work?', text: 'Fair credit models you can explain, the rules, and three ways to build one.' },
  { href: '/ai-work/ai-underwriting.html', tag: 'Head of underwriting', title: 'What can AI take off my team\'s desk?', text: 'The reading around a file, for lenders and insurers. The underwriter keeps the call.' },
  { href: '/ai-work/ai-invoice-processing.html', tag: 'Head of AP or finance ops', title: 'Can AI cut invoice cost without new fraud risk?', text: 'What invoice tools cost, what needs a person, and the fraud checks to keep.' },
];

// All 6 interactive tools surfaced on the homepage (clean 3x2 grid). Answers stay in the browser.
const tools = [
  { href: '/tools/ai-roi-calculator.html', tag: 'Calculator', title: 'AI ROI calculator', text: 'See whether one workflow pays back this year, using sourced labor and tool costs.' },
  { href: '/tools/ai-use-case-finder.html', tag: 'Interactive tool', title: 'AI use case finder', text: 'Answer six plain questions and get 3 to 5 practical starting projects for your team.' },
  { href: '/tools/ai-policy-generator.html', tag: 'Policy draft', title: 'AI policy generator', text: 'Build a plain-English company AI use policy tailored to your data and rules.' },
  { href: '/tools/ai-project-cost-estimator.html', tag: 'Cost estimator', title: 'AI agent cost estimator', text: 'Estimate monthly run cost and build effort for one workflow before you spend.' },
  { href: '/tools/ai-roadmap-builder.html', tag: 'Planner', title: 'AI roadmap builder', text: 'Turn your top gaps into a sequenced 90-day plan with owners and checkpoints.' },
  { href: '/tools/ai-training-plan.html', tag: 'Training plan', title: 'Employee AI training plan', text: 'See how many training hours each role needs, and which team should go first.' },
];

// 8 starter guides (clean 4x2 grid).
const finance = [
  { href: '/ai-consulting/ai-strategy-consulting.html', tag: 'Start here', title: 'AI strategy: where does AI pay first in your company?', text: 'What a good plan names, and what you should walk away with.' },
  { href: '/ai-consulting/ai-consulting-services.html', tag: 'Start here', title: 'AI consulting: is it worth it, and what does it cost?', text: 'What pays back first, and what help costs against hiring or software.' },
  { href: '/compare/build-vs-buy-ai.html', tag: 'Decision', title: 'Build vs buy AI: how should your team call it?', text: 'When off-the-shelf software wins, when custom work pays, and what each costs.' },
  { href: '/ai-work/ai-document-processing.html', tag: 'Documents', title: 'How accurate is AI on financial documents?', text: 'Our own test on 30 fund reports, answers locked before any tool ran.' },
  { href: '/ai-work/ai-invoice-processing.html', tag: 'Accounts payable', title: 'What does accounts payable automation cost, and what needs a person?', text: '13 tools and their prices. Exceptions and fraud still need a person.' },
  { href: '/ai-work/account-reconciliation-automation.html', tag: 'Month-end close', title: 'Will AI speed our close and pass audit?', text: 'What AI does, what auditors expect, and three ways to build it.' },
  { href: '/ai-work/ai-credit-scoring.html', tag: 'Lending', title: 'How do lenders keep AI credit scoring fair and explainable?', text: 'Credit models you can explain to an examiner, and the rules.' },
  { href: '/ai-work/ai-underwriting.html', tag: 'Underwriting', title: 'Can AI help underwriters, and who is using it?', text: 'Where AI pays in underwriting: the reading, not the decision.' },
];

const sources = [
  { n: 1, name: 'US Census Bureau, The Microstructure of AI Diffusion, working paper CES-WP-26-25 (April 2026)', url: 'https://www.census.gov/library/working-papers/2026/adrm/CES-WP-26-25.html', what: '66% of firms that use AI use it only to help with tasks; AI-related job cuts happened at 2% of firms.' },
  { n: 2, name: 'Zavient FinExtractBench (November 2026)', url: '/ai-work/ai-document-processing.html#own-data', what: 'Our benchmark of 30 private fund reports, 781 pages, with every answer written by hand and locked before any tool ran.' },
  { n: 3, name: 'APQC, total cost to process accounts payable', url: 'https://www.apqc.org/what-we-do/benchmarking/open-standards-benchmarking/measures/total-cost-perform-process-process', what: 'Median all-in cost of $6.00 per invoice, across 4,821 companies.' },
  { n: 4, name: 'Newman, JAMA (1995), interpreting small numerators', url: 'https://jamanetwork.com/journals/jama/article-abstract/389714', what: 'With zero errors in N tries, the true error rate can still be up to about 3 in N.' },
];
const fn = (n) => `#fn-${n}`;
const updated = '27 November 2026';
---
<Base title="AI for every kind of work: where should your company start? | Zavient" description="Zavient helps companies of 40 to 500 people put AI to work in any function and any industry. Pick your kind of work or industry, try a free tool, or book a free 30-minute diagnostic." canonical="https://zavient.com/" updated="2026-11-27">
  <header class="article-hero"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="label">Zavient &middot; AI that helps your team do more</div>
    <h1>AI for every kind of work: where should your company <span class="hl">start?</span></h1>
    <span class="bluf-label">Bottom line</span>
    <div class="bluf">
      <ul>
        <li>We help companies of 40 to 500 people put AI to work in any function and any industry.</li>
        <li>AI does the reading, matching and first draft. Your people keep the decision.</li>
        <li>Free 30-minute diagnostic, any kind of work: you leave knowing buy or build, what to test and rough cost.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:22px;"><a class="btn-gold" href="#diagnostic">Book a free 30-minute diagnostic &rarr;</a></p>
    <p class="diag-nudge">Not ready to talk? <a href="/ai-readiness-assessment.html">Take the 3-minute AI readiness check</a> or <a href="#tools">use one of our 6 free tools</a>. Your answers stay in your browser.</p>
  </div></header>

  <article class="article-body"><div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="role">Start with your role</h2>
    <p>Pick your seat. Each card answers the first question people in that seat ask.</p>
    <div class="hub-grid">
      {roles.map((k) => (
        <a class="hub-card" href={k.href}>
          <span class="hub-tag">{k.tag}</span>
          <h3>{k.title}</h3>
          <p>{k.text}</p>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="diag-nudge">Head of another division? <a href="#diagnostic">Bring one workflow to the free 30-minute diagnostic &rarr;</a></p>

    <h2 id="tools">Free interactive tools</h2>
    <p>Run the numbers on your own team before talking to any vendor. Every tool runs in your browser with no signup.</p>
    <div class="hub-grid">
      {tools.map((t) => (
        <a class="hub-card" href={t.href}>
          <span class="hub-tag">{t.tag}</span>
          <h3>{t.title}</h3>
          <p>{t.text}</p>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="diag-nudge">Want a quick baseline across the whole company? <a href="/ai-readiness-assessment.html">Take the 3-minute AI readiness check &rarr;</a></p>

    <h2 id="work">Find your kind of work or industry</h2>
    <p>Pick your kind of work or your industry. Each card opens a guide.</p>
    <div class="hub-grid">
      {kinds.map((k) => (
        <a class="hub-card" href={k.href}>
          <span class="hub-tag">{k.tag}</span>
          <h3>{k.title}</h3>
          <p>{k.text}</p>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="diag-nudge">No guide yet for {noGuideYet}? <a href="#diagnostic">Bring it to the free 30-minute diagnostic &rarr;</a></p>

    <h2 id="guides">Guides you can read today</h2>
    <p>Each guide answers one question about one kind of work. Each covers: who stays in the loop, cost, rules, buy or build.</p>
    <div class="hub-grid">
      {finance.map((w) => (
        <a class="hub-card" href={w.href}>
          <span class="hub-tag">{w.tag}</span>
          <h3>{w.title}</h3>
          <p>{w.text}</p>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="diag-nudge">Looking for another workflow or industry? <a href="/ai-work.html">Search all 61 guides and tools &rarr;</a></p>

    <h2 id="how">How we work with you</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Free 30-minute diagnostic.</strong> Bring one workflow from any part of the business, and what it costs you today. You leave with our read on buy or build, and what to test first.</li>
      <li><strong>A 30-day sprint on the work that pays first.</strong> Fixed scope. You get written specs, what to build and how to test it, that your team or a vendor builds from.</li>
      <li><strong>Your team runs it.</strong> You own the specs and the results. We advise while it ships, then step back.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>What each step includes is on our <a href="/about.html#engagements">About page</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="who">Who you work with</h2>
    <p>You work directly with an experienced operator, not a rotating bench of junior analysts.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>20 years across B2B software, production ML and private equity.</strong> Includes COO turnaround experience and independent sponsor deals.</li>
      <li><strong>Independent advice only.</strong> We sell no software and take no vendor referral fees.</li>
      <li><strong>Specs your team owns.</strong> Every sprint leaves clear build specs, benchmarks and a 90-day plan with no lock-in.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Read the founder's full operating record on our <a href="/about.html#founder">About page</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="people">Your team stays in charge</h2>
    <p>Our focus is AI that helps people do more, not AI that replaces them. Most firms already use it that way.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Most AI use is help, not replacement.</strong> 66% of firms that use AI use it only to help with tasks<sup class="fn"><a href={fn(1)} aria-label="Source 1">1</a></sup>.</li>
      <li><strong>Few firms cut jobs over AI.</strong> Just 2% did<sup class="fn"><a href={fn(1)} aria-label="Source 1">1</a></sup>.</li>
      <li><strong>People keep the decision.</strong> AI reads, matches and drafts. A person approves the loan, the claim or the payment.</li>
      <li><strong>Every answer can be checked.</strong> We pick tools that show where each answer came from.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="proof">How we check our numbers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>We write the right answers first, then test.</strong> On 30 fund reports, the two best AI models made zero mistakes<sup class="fn"><a href={fn(2)} aria-label="Source 2">2</a></sup>.</li>
      <li><strong>We count the whole cost.</strong> The median company spends $6.00 to process one invoice, all in<sup class="fn"><a href={fn(3)} aria-label="Source 3">3</a></sup>.</li>
      <li><strong>30 reports is a small test.</strong> The true miss rate could still be up to 1 in 10<sup class="fn"><a href={fn(4)} aria-label="Source 4">4</a></sup>. So we re-test on your files before you buy.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>How we source and check every page is on our <a href="/about.html#method">About page</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="data-evaluation">Data evaluation before AI licensing</h2>
    <p>Companies considering licensing internal records to AI buyers need an independent check first. We build a counted inventory and benchmark one model with and without your records.</p>
    <p>You keep the written evaluation and decide whether licensing makes sense. <a href="#diagnostic">Ask about a data evaluation below &rarr;</a></p>

    <h2 id="sources">Sources</h2>
    <ol class="sources">
      {sources.map((s) => <li id={`fn-${s.n}`}><a href={s.url}>{s.name}</a>. {s.what}</li>)}
    </ol>
    <p class="byline">By <a href="/about.html">Zavient</a> &middot; updated {updated}</p>
  </div></article>

  <ConsultingCta job="AI in any part of your business" heading="Not sure where to start? Get a free diagnostic" />

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'Zavient',
    legalName: 'Zavient LLC',
    url: 'https://zavient.com/',
    logo: 'https://zavient.com/favicon.svg',
    description: 'AI consulting for companies of 40 to 500 people, across every kind of work and every industry.',
    contactPoint: { '@type': 'ContactPoint', contactType: 'sales', email: 'hello@zavient.com' },
  })} />
</Base>
